-- title:
--   Uniqueness of formally smooth lifts along a nilpotent ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and $I \subseteq R$ an ideal which is nilpotent, i.e. $I^n = 0$ for some $n$. Let $A$, $A'$, $A_0$ be commutative $R$-algebras, with $A$ and $A'$ formally smooth over $R$. Suppose given $R$-algebra homomorphisms $g : A \to A_0$ and $g' : A' \to A_0$, both surjective, whose kernels are exactly the ideals generated by the image of $I$, that is $\ker g = I \cdot A = (\mathrm{alg\,map}\ R\ A)(I)A$ and $\ker g' = I \cdot A'$ (in Lean, $I.map$ of the respective structure maps). The conclusion is that there exists an $R$-algebra isomorphism $e : A \simeq A'$ compatible with the two maps to $A_0$, in the sense that the composite of $e$ with $g'$ equals $g$, i.e. $g' \circ e = g$ as $R$-algebra homomorphisms $A \to A_0$. Thus any two formally smooth $R$-algebra lifts of $A_0$ with kernels $IA$ and $IA'$ are isomorphic over $A_0$; no uniqueness of $e$ is asserted.
--
--   This is the standard uniqueness (up to non-canonical isomorphism) of a smooth lift of an algebra along a nilpotent thickening of the base, the affine case of the deformation-theoretic statement that smooth lifts are unique over the reduction. It is used to deduce the corresponding assertion for smooth morphisms of schemes in the affine pullback situation, [`AlgebraicGeometry.Smooth.exists_iso_hom_comp_eq_of_isPullback_of_isAffine_of_isNilpotent`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Smooth.exists_iso_hom_comp_eq_of_isPullback_of_isAffine_of_isNilpotent).
